# Local development variables — copy to `.dev.vars` and fill in.
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# `.dev.vars` is gitignored and read by `wrangler dev`. Nothing here is a
# production credential: every value below is either optional or yours alone.
# Real secrets live in Cloudflare (`wrangler secret put --env <env>`) and in
# GitHub Environment secrets. See docs/DEVOPS.md > Secrets.

# --- Google sign-in (#27) -----------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Leave both empty and the Google routes disable themselves rather
# than failing, so a fresh clone runs with no credentials at all.
# Create at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#   Authorised origin:     http://localhost:8787
#   Authorised redirect:   http://localhost:8787/api/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Google Maps (#31) --------------------------------------------------------
# Optional, and read by Vite at build time — so it belongs in a `.env.local`
# too if you build rather than run `wrangler dev`. The wizard's venue picker
# degrades to typed coordinates without it, which is exactly what a preview
# deployment does, so a fresh clone still works end to end.
#
# It is a build-time public value baked into the bundle, so it MUST be
# HTTP-referrer restricted, with a separate key per environment
# (docs/DEVOPS.md > Secrets).
#   Local key referrers: http://localhost:5173/*, http://localhost:8787/*
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# --- Not set here -------------------------------------------------------------
# DB, SETTINGS, MEDIA, ENVIRONMENT and OFFER_API_URL are bindings and vars from
# wrangler.jsonc, not secrets. `npm run db:reset` builds the local D1 and seeds
# it; you do not need any Cloudflare access to develop against local resources.
